From 3f4e7f6ba3505bcc68d9797ba19dba5ba79cfc91 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Justin <justurn@live.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 15:30:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Zeppelin F-234: prebuilt HD grass shaders (Forever grass with
 wxl wind on Vulkan), GPU frame time and settings in the perf log

- HD::ShaderPrebuilt: a material's bytecode from Vulkan\hd-blobs\<material>-<vs|ps>-<a>-<b>-<key>.bin (MPQ first),
  key = FNV-1a of its HLSL; HdGrass uses it before compiling, so every machine draws the bytes the Vulkan manifest
  knows (a runtime compile depends on the player's d3dcompiler_47); hdShaderDump writes the keyed names
- g_gxGpuFrame (GxSeam): the GPU frame time, from wxl GetFrameStats on Vulkan (HdVulkanPerf) and timestamp queries
  Present to Present on D3D9 / D3D9Ex (GpuFrameTimerD3d9, armed only while hdCataRenderPerf is on)
- CataRenderPerf.log: a session header (renderer, adapter, GPU timer, settings), one stamped line per window (FPS,
  frame-time avg/p50/p95/p99/max, CPU world/scene, GPU avg/max), and a line whenever a setting changes

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UHcJJVC4feQ4s15e9bNRoN
